    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> be three non-zero non-coplanar vectors and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> be three vectors defined as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mspace width=\"0.222em\"/></math>\r<p>If the volume of parallelepiped determined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> is <math><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></semantics></math> and that of the parallelepiped determined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> is <math><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></semantics></math> then,&nbsp;<math><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">KV</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></semantics></math> implies that the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> is</p>\r"
